from pathlib import Path
import pandas as pd,json
P=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
assert (P/'PIPELINE_COMPLETE').exists(),'Do not publish incomplete SPY results'
a=json.loads((P/'audit.json').read_text());assert a['completed_batch_requests']==23
h=pd.read_csv(P/'hedge_scores.csv');o=pd.read_csv(P/'option_crp_scores.csv');c=pd.read_csv(P/'company_portfolio_scores.csv');f=pd.read_csv(P/'liquid_futures_comparisons.csv');g=pd.read_csv(P/'volatility_gate_scores.csv')
def table(x):return x.to_markdown(index=False,floatfmt='.2f')
parts=['# Direct rebalancing mechanism research\n\nCompleted research replays; no production changes or orders. Prior bot/sleeve capital-allocation work is excluded from these conclusions. The question tested here is whether inventory rebalancing improves an existing strategy or a derivative implementation.']
parts.append('**Recommendation.** Do not deploy any of these tested extensions. Reject the trend inventory overlays, the independently checked futures pairs as robust rebalancing improvements, and the tested SPY gamma-hedging/call-put rebalancing designs. Keep CI/YUMC long-call rebalancing only as a research lead: its incremental P&L survived three months and doubled commissions, but roughly 45% within-month drawdowns make it unsuitable as the relatively safe implementation sought earlier. A positive increment in this small leveraged experiment is not a validated trading edge.')
parts.append('**Integration inside the trend bot.** Replayed January 2011–July 2026 baseline, Ridge10 and Width20 with original entries, maximum positions and exits. Retained one-third or two-thirds core inventory; trimmed/restored the remainder at 0.5, 1 or 2 trailing-ATR spacings. Decisions use the preceding native 15-minute bar and fills use the next open. The original stop remains active. Compared all six variants with unchanged and simply reduced positions, at two cost levels. All six variants underperform the full parent across all three parents over the full sample. For baseline at the first cost level, unchanged P&L was $16,821; overlay P&L ranged from −$24,376 to −$2,104. For Ridge10, unchanged was $44,395 versus $6,169–$28,192. This integration sells the exposure needed to capture sustained trends and adds turnover. Parent replays match archived results within $0.0000001. Native large-contract bars use the stored micro economics where applicable; periods before micro launch are proxies. ATR is calculated from 80 preceding 15-minute bars, not assumed identical to every parent indicator.')
parts.append('The continuation also tested 12 choppy-path-gated rules for each parent and cost combination: only trim when 20-bar path efficiency is at most 0.3 or 0.5, restoring the original target when directional. This improved some overlays but none exceeded its full parent over the complete sample. Baseline’s best gated result at the first cost level was $1,813, versus the unchanged $16,821. Across the unconditional and gated grids, 108 overlay configurations were evaluated. The gated-parent controls also match exactly.')
parts.append('**Futures implementation.** Screened all 153 eligible pairs from 18 available markets over January 2019–June 2026. Kept daily/weekly schedules, whole/fractional sizing and both cost levels. Fixed-notional and equity-compounding versions are separate. The original gold source proved sparse, so its apparent edge was not accepted. Purchased volume-selected hourly ES, NQ, GC, HG and SI, rebuilt roll-adjusted P&L and retested all ten combinations. The following table uses whole contracts, daily rebalancing, doubled fees/slippage and $1m initial collateral. “Increment” is relative to rolling the initial contract quantities unchanged. Large outright profits primarily reflect the market exposures; they do not establish a rebalancing edge.')
parts.append(table(f[f.integer & f.cost.eq(2)&f.design.eq('daily')&f.period.eq('all')][['a','b','net','increment','drawdown_pct']].assign(drawdown_pct=lambda x:100*x.drawdown_pct)))
parts.append('None of these ten pairs has positive incremental P&L in both chronological periods across whole/fractional sizing and both costs. NQ/SI illustrates the issue: its small full-period whole-contract advantage does not survive the recent period or fractional sizing at higher cost. Source panels include roll approximations and vendor-degraded dates. Cash interest is excluded; margin is only stress-tested, not an exchange liquidation simulation. Negative oil observations were retained in the 153-pair screen, with a universal bounded sizing divisor; futures crossing zero are not exact positive-price stock CRPs. The fresh five-market results supersede claims based on their old source files.')
parts.append('**SPY options: real premiums plus inventory hedging.** Buy one ATM call and put at 10:01 asks; exit at 14:45 bids, or 15 minutes before an early close. Select using 09:59 stock close and the available 10:00 chain. Fit straddle IV to observed mids to estimate delta; execute hedge changes at the following stock minute open. Test unhedged, entry-only delta, 5/15/60-minute updates and 5/10/20-share bands. Actual option P&L comes from quotes, not model values. Base costs are $0.65 per option contract per side and 1bp per stock dollar traded; stress doubles option fees and uses 3bp. Values below are dollars per one-call/one-put episode, with observable terminal quotes. They are not account returns; short-stock collateral has not been treated as free capital.')
parts.append(table(h[h.symbol.eq('spy')&h.period.eq('all')&h.case.eq('base')&h.coverage.eq('complete_exit')][['tenor','design','n','mean_option_pnl','mean_hedge_pnl','mean','mean_increment']]))
parts.append('“Mean increment” compares with entry-only delta hedging on matching dates. Hedge P&L already deducts stock trading costs. Missing terminal quotes are zero-valued in the separate conservative table; complete-quote and ≥95%-valid-delta sensitivities are retained. The straddle-IV delta model uses zero rates/dividends and is a short-horizon approximation, not a calibrated American volatility surface. Trades with invalid delta estimates skip that update. [OIC explains gamma](https://prd-web.optionseducation.org/advancedconcepts/gamma); the test measures whether that convexity repays its price.')
parts.append('The SPY decision is rejection: all tested rehedging schedules have negative full-sample average net P&L at both costs, and the scheduled 15/60-minute variants are negative in each chronological period. The variance-price gates remain negative over the full sample. Freezing IV at entry or estimating delta from a parity-implied forward does not reverse the result. These checks reject the tested long-gamma implementations, not every conceivable options strategy.')
parts.append('**Independent IWM check.** Same mechanism and assumptions on the broader existing IWM cache:')
parts.append(table(h[h.symbol.eq('iwm')&h.period.eq('all')&h.case.eq('base')&h.coverage.eq('complete_exit')][['tenor','design','n','mean','mean_increment']]))
parts.append('**Volatility-price gate.** Tested always entering and forecast-variance/IV-variance thresholds 1, 1.25 and 1.5. The forecast uses half the first 30 minutes of intraday RV and half the previous 20 sessions’ later-session RV, excluding overnight returns. All schedules, thresholds, dates and cost cases remain in volatility_gate_scores.csv. This is exploratory screening; neither a single positive cell nor a bootstrap interval selected after this search establishes an edge. Chronological splits are diagnostics, not pristine holdouts.')
parts.append(table(g[g.symbol.eq('SPY')&g.period.eq('all')&g.case.eq('stress')&g.coverage.eq('complete_exit')&g.design.isin(['static_delta','every15','every60'])][['threshold','tenor','design','n','mean']]))
parts.append('**Call/put value rebalancing on one underlying.** Separately tested $10,000 50/50 call/put premium-value portfolios, holding versus 15/60-minute rebalancing. A second control completes the initial fixed quantities when quote capacity permits and then holds. The table uses whole contracts, base costs and only dates on which all compared controls liquidate within terminal quoted depth. This selection is not a deployable entry rule; the all-date conservative results are also retained. Equal premium weights do not mean equal delta exposure.')
parts.append(table(o[o.integer&o.period.eq('all')&o.case.eq('base')&o.coverage.eq('both_liquidated')&o.design.isin(['rebalance15','rebalance60'])][['symbol','tenor','design','n','mean','mean_increment','mean_fill_increment']]))
parts.append('**Options implementation of CI/YUMC.** At the beginning of each month, choose near-ATM calls with 30–75 days to expiry using the prior stock close; fill next session. Rebalance premium values 50/50 daily or weekly, holding those contracts through month-end. Each month starts with $10,000 independently. These are three reset experiments, not a compounded quarterly account. Orders respect sampled sizes. Exit over 15:45–15:59 month-end quotes; all final whole-contract books liquidate in this replay. Repeated quote snapshots assume displayed liquidity can replenish, without own-order market impact. The single-quote depth-bound results are preserved separately. February has one missing intermediate quote day and March two; those days skip trading rather than disappear from the calendar.')
parts.append(table(c[c.integer&c.instrument.eq('long_calls')][['month','case','design','net','drawdown_pct']].assign(drawdown_pct=lambda x:100*x.drawdown_pct)))
parts.append('Daily rebalancing beats both hold and fill-initial in all three months at both commission levels. At doubled commissions, the monthly increments over holding are $104.00, $1,952.20 and $135.80. The daily call book still suffered roughly 45% within-month peak-to-trough drawdowns at daily quote marks. This is a high-risk mechanism experiment, not the relatively safe implementation sought earlier and not an investable long-run edge. Much of the absolute call gain may be directional leverage. A fair next validation needs a longer fixed sample, adverse regimes, delta/risk-matched stock and option controls, and stronger execution modeling; do not select a new pair or expiry using these three winning increments.')
parts.append('A funded call-plus-strike-cash diagnostic reduced drawdowns to roughly 2–3% in the tested months, but whole-contract daily and weekly results were identical to holding: the rebalance did not change quantities. That lower risk is a payoff/funding change, not a newly demonstrated rebalancing edge.')
parts.append('Funded synthetic longs were also tested with $100,000 and strike cash included. Their strongest February comparison weakens against simply completing the initial orders: base daily P&L $3,516 versus fill-initial $3,744. These are pricing/accounting diagnostics, not recommended implementations. Early assignment, dividends, financing and exercise are omitted. American short puts can be assigned before expiration. [OIC assignment reference](https://www.optionseducation.org/referencelibrary/faq/options-assignment).')
parts.append('**Coverage, verification and spending.**\n\n```json\n'+json.dumps({k:a[k] for k in ['completed_batch_requests','expected_batch_requests','fresh_spy_files','spy','iwm']},indent=2)+'\n```\n\nTen accounting/parity checks pass (verification.json). All result grids, rejected variants, acquisition ledgers and source-code scripts are retained. Budget reservations across prior and current work total $'+f"{a['reserved_total_usd']:.2f}"+' against the original $120 ceiling, including the interrupted request. Reservations are not the account balance. Vendor batch charges and streaming estimates are separated in cost_reconciliation.csv; the credit-balance endpoint has not been verified.')
parts.append('**Interpretation of Cover.** These are mechanism extensions, not a reproduction of Cover’s universal-portfolio theorem. A universal portfolio’s asymptotic comparison is with the best constant-rebalanced portfolio selected in hindsight; it does not say any chosen pair or derivative will deliver a specified return after costs. [Cover’s Stanford portfolio publications](https://isl.stanford.edu/~cover/portfolio-theory.html). A 74-fold result over 22 years corresponds to about 21.6% compound annual growth, not 70% annually. Expiring options introduce premium decay and a changing payoff, so the original example cannot simply be transferred by substituting option tickers.')
parts.append('**Files.**\n\n'+'\n'.join(f'- [{name}]({P/name})' for name in ['inventory_comparisons.csv','futures_crp_comparisons.csv','liquid_futures_comparisons.csv','hedge_scores.csv','option_crp_scores.csv','volatility_gate_scores.csv','delta_sensitivity_scores.csv','company_portfolio_scores.csv','cost_reconciliation.csv','verification.json','PROTOCOL.md']))
(P/'REPORT.md').write_text('\n\n'.join(parts));print('REPORT.md written')
